WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.790
Hiya, everybody. Welcome to a new episode of Easy English.

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:06.790
So after a long time away, we're finally back in the UK.

3
00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:13.150
So I thought I'd quickly nip into Brighton and ask a simple question to the people wandering around: what are you up to today?

4
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.310
So, let's head into Brighton. Here we go.

5
00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:19.990
What are you two up to today in Brighton?

6
00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.790
We're just shopping, mostly. - Yeah.

7
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.810
Yeah? - Just heading around.

8
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.990
We're trying to find a thrift shop at the moment.

9
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:28.930
What are you two up to today in Brighton?

10
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.210
We are just on our lunch break. - Just getting lunch, yeah.

11
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.670
We're going to get some sushi, actually.

12
00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.270
Can you tell me what you're up to today in Brighton?

13
00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.650
We are just wasting a day, basically, waiting for a ferry.

14
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.370
What are you up to in Brighton today?

15
00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.890
Just wandering aimlessly around The Lanes today.

16
00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.590
So we're here for the beach, obviously.

17
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.330
I think everyone kind of comes to Brighton for the beach.

18
00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.590
But we're en route now to an Italian restaurant,

19
00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.330
and we're here for a concert,

20
00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.170
so we've stayed effectively for the weekend.

21
00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.690
And we're going to enjoy a nice pop concert in Chalk, just down the road.

22
00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.570
So it's not far from here. But generally, enjoying the sun.

23
00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:08.430
Where we live has very poor weather at the minute,

24
00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:13.710
so we've come for a bit of an escape, I think, is probably how to round it up. - Okay, a getaway.

25
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.610
What are you up to in Brighton today?

26
00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:21.810
So we've come to Brighton today to visit with my niece and my sister, who are over from France.

27
00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.790
We're going down The Lanes, doing some shopping.

28
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.410
Now we're heading off to the beach.

29
00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.010
Just had something to eat.

30
00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:30.433
Probably get a snack on the way back,

31
00:01:30.433 --> 00:01:32.473
and then we'll drive back to Kent, which is where I live.

32
00:01:32.473 --> 00:01:36.033
So I'm with my boyfriend at the moment, who is just out of frame,

33
00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.653
because he didn't want to be in the interview.

34
00:01:37.653 --> 00:01:40.533
And we... - Heckling from the side. - Yeah.

35
00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:44.493
We just went to the Hello Kitty cafe.

36
00:01:44.493 --> 00:01:50.053
We had some food, and now I think we're going to... we're pottery painting.

37
00:01:50.053 --> 00:01:51.693
And then after that... yeah, I'm not sure.

38
00:01:51.693 --> 00:01:55.553
Can you explain what a thrift shop is?

39
00:01:55.553 --> 00:01:59.973
It's like a shop with secondhand items, mostly clothing.

40
00:01:59.973 --> 00:02:03.413
Yeah, there's a vegan sushi restaurant there, so that's where we're going.

41
00:02:03.413 --> 00:02:05.213
Okay, do you go there often?

42
00:02:05.213 --> 00:02:09.213
Yeah, it's my... when I want a nice lunch, that's my treat. - Yeah, exactly.

43
00:02:09.213 --> 00:02:11.653
And today feels like one of those days to get a treat.

44
00:02:11.653 --> 00:02:13.373
And what's your order?

45
00:02:13.373 --> 00:02:14.933
I get... so they do sushi burritos.

46
00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:18.933
So it's like a burrito with sushi, but it's all vegan,

47
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:25.253
so I normally get... they have a wrap, which is like sesame chicken, but it's not real chicken.

48
00:02:25.253 --> 00:02:27.273
Yeah, that's what I'm going to order, probably.

49
00:02:27.273 --> 00:02:31.453
I actually haven't decided yet, so maybe I'll just figure it out once I get there.

50
00:02:31.453 --> 00:02:33.493
Okay. Oh, this one behind us, Happy Maki?

51
00:02:33.493 --> 00:02:35.713
Yeah, that's where we're going. - That's the one.

52
00:02:35.713 --> 00:02:39.493
Oh, really? - Yeah, we're getting a nine o'clock ferry over to Santander,

53
00:02:39.493 --> 00:02:41.473
and we had a day to kind of kill.

54
00:02:41.473 --> 00:02:48.873
So we thought we'd come to Brighton, do a bit of shopping, looking around, browsing for old books.

55
00:02:48.873 --> 00:02:50.473
You've come to the best place to look for old stuff.

56
00:02:50.473 --> 00:02:54.193
I bought some fabulous fabric as well, and I've seen...

57
00:02:54.193 --> 00:02:59.256
there's two shops I need to go back in and have a look at fabrics, because I sew, so I love sewing.

58
00:02:59.256 --> 00:02:59.616
Okay, great.

59
00:02:59.616 --> 00:03:01.856
And next, you're off to pottery class.

60
00:03:01.856 --> 00:03:04.256
Yes, we're pottery painting. - Pottery painting. Big day.

61
00:03:04.256 --> 00:03:07.676
And this is like a hobby you have, or a one-off thing?

62
00:03:07.676 --> 00:03:11.876
No, we just kind of like... I don't know, usually our schedules, like, don't align super well.

63
00:03:11.876 --> 00:03:17.236
But today we were like, oh, we have like the whole day. Let's just do a bunch of, like, fun stuff.

64
00:03:17.236 --> 00:03:19.896
Especially 'cause it's a Monday, it's not, like, super busy in town at the moment.

65
00:03:19.896 --> 00:03:24.536
So we thought, let's do some whimsical activities. - Sounds whimsical.

66
00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:25.956
What do you two do for work?

67
00:03:25.956 --> 00:03:30.236
We both work in marketing... marketing, in the same company, at William Reed.

68
00:03:30.236 --> 00:03:31.916
Okay. You're happy at your job? Like your job?

69
00:03:31.916 --> 00:03:36.956
Yeah. - Yeah, it's fun. - We run events, so we do marketing for events.

70
00:03:36.956 --> 00:03:39.736
Do you live in Brighton? - No, I live south London.

71
00:03:39.736 --> 00:03:44.996
Okay. - Yeah, yeah. - And how long are you down for? How long are you down in Brighton for?

72
00:03:44.996 --> 00:03:47.036
Just the weekend, three days.

73
00:03:47.036 --> 00:03:50.596
But my girlfriend went to uni here, so she's kind of...

74
00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:54.416
I've come here a couple of times, but she's showing me around.

75
00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:55.976
And are you from Brighton?

76
00:03:55.976 --> 00:03:58.316
I'm from Canterbury, in Kent, originally,

77
00:03:58.316 --> 00:04:03.856
but I've lived in Brighton for, like, four years now, I want to say.

78
00:04:03.856 --> 00:04:07.256
And I actually got my... my uni results today.

79
00:04:07.256 --> 00:04:09.936
Passed. Got my degree... - Well done! - Got a 2:1. Very happy with that.

80
00:04:09.936 --> 00:04:14.576
But yeah, I'm just going to try and live here as long as I can, because I like it.

81
00:04:14.576 --> 00:04:17.516
Oh, really? You'd like to stay? - Yeah, I love Brighton. It's really, really nice.

82
00:04:17.516 --> 00:04:18.996
Where are you going for food in a minute?

83
00:04:18.996 --> 00:04:20.896
Ask Italian. - Ask Italian, yeah.

84
00:04:20.896 --> 00:04:25.796
Yeah, we've got a voucher, so we want the money off. - It's okay.

85
00:04:25.796 --> 00:04:29.179
Ask Italian's pretty good anyway, even if you don't have a voucher, I think, no?

86
00:04:29.179 --> 00:04:33.339
And, out of interest, what are you watching? You're going to a concert tomorrow? - We are.

87
00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.819
We're going to watch an artist called Peach PRC.

88
00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:38.519
So we're going to have a good time.

89
00:04:38.519 --> 00:04:40.259
And you get a nice long lunch break?

90
00:04:40.259 --> 00:04:44.939
We get an hour. - Get an hour. So we literally just like... on our way.

91
00:04:44.939 --> 00:04:47.079
It's like a grab-and-go situation.

92
00:04:47.079 --> 00:04:48.499
I won't keep you any longer then, let you get to it.

93
00:04:48.499 --> 00:04:52.599
So you have a 9 pm ferry... from where, though? Not from Brighton? - From Portsmouth.

94
00:04:52.599 --> 00:04:54.979
Oh, so you're going back to... - Yeah, back to Portsmouth.

95
00:04:54.979 --> 00:04:59.439
So it's a little bit random, but I didn't want to go to Southampton or Portsmouth.

96
00:04:59.439 --> 00:05:03.279
I wanted to go further afield, and Winchester we know like the back of our hand.

97
00:05:03.279 --> 00:05:05.679
So we thought, Brighton!

98
00:05:05.679 --> 00:05:08.099
And then, so I'm guessing you're getting, like, an overnight sleeper ferry thing?

99
00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:11.059
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

100
00:05:11.059 --> 00:05:14.219
Walk our legs off today and basically put them up tomorrow on the ferry.

101
00:05:14.219 --> 00:05:17.199
Oh my God, you're going to be knackered. - Yeah, I think so.

102
00:05:17.199 --> 00:05:20.139
And how long is the ferry? - About 30 hours. - Oh, wow!

103
00:05:20.139 --> 00:05:22.519
Okay, so over a couple of days? - Yeah, yeah, yeah. - Amazing!

104
00:05:22.519 --> 00:05:25.819
So we land in Spain on Wednesday morning. - Wow!

105
00:05:25.819 --> 00:05:27.599
Well, have a great time. - Thank you!

106
00:05:27.599 --> 00:05:30.419
And how does Brighton compare to your home... to Cardiff?

107
00:05:30.419 --> 00:05:31.899
Nothing beats where we're from, I don't think.

108
00:05:31.899 --> 00:05:35.599
I think I'll always have a connection to that place.

109
00:05:35.599 --> 00:05:38.179
But it's always good to see different things.

110
00:05:38.179 --> 00:05:40.959
This is our first... first step of travelling, really.

111
00:05:40.959 --> 00:05:42.939
We're going to go broader, obviously, later on.

112
00:05:42.939 --> 00:05:47.819
We are actually planning to go on a trip to Japan in a few years, for our shared big birthdays.

113
00:05:47.819 --> 00:05:51.579
So, you know, it's all in the works, but we're easing into it at the moment.

114
00:05:51.579 --> 00:05:55.100
Yeah, nice. Great! I hope you have a nice time in Brighton. - Thank you!
